    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f063e98_8b20eb01",
        "filename": "system/vendor_libs/test_vendor_lib/packets/link_layer_packets.pdl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T21:56:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good reminder. I think it would be better to add more types here.\n\nWe could follow along with the table in the spec \nTable 7.2: Advertising_Event_Properties values for legacy PDUs\n\nADV_IND 0b00010011 (0x13)\nADV_DIRECT_IND 0b00010101 (0x15)\nADV_DIRECT_IND 0b00011101 (0x1d)\nADV_SCAN_IND 0b00010010 (0x12)\nADV_NONCONN_IND 0b00010000 (0x10)\nAnd we could use the other bits like\nADV_CONNECTABLE 0x01\n...\n\nOr we could use the LMP definition.",
      "revId": "26da656d4cc84ec4e778e21df1a6ade4775f4c61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9309fce2_717b7f38",
        "filename": "system/vendor_libs/test_vendor_lib/packets/link_layer_packets.pdl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T23:10:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is that these values are used in HCI commands and events, while LMP values are hidden. My initial move was to add an alias ADV_DIREC._IND_LOW \u003d 4, but that is not supported by the PDL generator. I think it is possible to modify PDL to allow this though, what do you think ?",
      "parentUuid": "4f063e98_8b20eb01",
      "revId": "26da656d4cc84ec4e778e21df1a6ade4775f4c61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c177ad1a_59cd8d72",
        "filename": "system/vendor_libs/test_vendor_lib/packets/link_layer_packets.pdl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T23:27:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is the link layer, the values don\u0027t have to be tied to HCI commands.  We can also have a bit mask of properties (no need for \"legacy\"), and translate from that when we need it.  I guess we only need these three bits:\n\n0 Connectable advertising\n1 Scannable advertising\n2 Directed advertising\n\nWe don\u0027t need to know at the link layer if it\u0027s legacy, high-duty-cycle, anonymous, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "9309fce2_717b7f38",
      "revId": "26da656d4cc84ec4e778e21df1a6ade4775f4c61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ceb8e866_2870364c",
        "filename": "system/vendor_libs/test_vendor_lib/packets/link_layer_packets.pdl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T16:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would rather keep the current AdvertisementType type in link_layer_packets.pdl to spare the additional conversions in IncomingLeAdvertisementPacket and LeSetAdvertisingParameters. \n\nI do think it will become necessary to rewrite the type to support extended advertising PDUs. This would be done in another CL.",
      "parentUuid": "c177ad1a_59cd8d72",
      "revId": "26da656d4cc84ec4e778e21df1a6ade4775f4c61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
